1
00:00:02,102 --> 00:00:03,434
JIM: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,866
You are a cop in
everything but name.

3
00:00:06,106 --> 00:00:07,768
Saving Gotham's
not my job anymore.

4
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:10,773
ALICE: <i>If a person comes into
contact with my blood, it changes them.</i>

5
00:00:11,111 --> 00:00:13,012
<i>It affects every
person differently.</i>

6
00:00:13,313 --> 00:00:16,147
I won. They really want me as
mayor. How did you know I would win?

7
00:00:16,383 --> 00:00:19,512
I believe in you, Oswald. Even
when you don't believe in yourself.

8
00:00:19,953 --> 00:00:22,013
- Miss Kringle?
- No, my name's Isabella.

9
00:00:22,623 --> 00:00:25,422
You remind me of
someone. I'm Edward Nygma.

10
00:00:25,626 --> 00:00:26,924
JIM: <i>Past is the past.</i>

11
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:29,005
DR. THOMPKINS: <i>I know
that we can't change the past,</i>

12
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:31,430
<i>but there's a difference
between moving on and letting go.</i>

13
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,496
Who do you love?

14
00:00:33,834 --> 00:00:37,737
Or I shoot both of them,
which would be such a thrill.

15
00:00:38,338 --> 00:00:39,567
- Kill Lee.
- (GASPS)

16
00:00:43,277 --> 00:00:45,576
(EKG MACHINE BEEPING)

17
00:00:48,448 --> 00:00:50,542
I'm so sorry this happened.

18
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:57,081
Stop the press.

19
00:00:58,592 --> 00:01:03,428
Tough guy Jim Gordon
sheds tear for Valerie Vale.

20
00:01:07,601 --> 00:01:08,762
How're you feeling?

21
00:01:10,103 --> 00:01:14,040
Like a bullet went through my insides.
You don't have any whiskey, do you?

22
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:15,841
Sorry.

23
00:01:16,043 --> 00:01:19,480
You get a girl shot and you
don't even bring her booze.

24
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:22,048
You got a lot of nerve.

25
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,742
I never meant
for you to get hurt.

26
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:31,320
You did. You wanted to save Lee.

27
00:01:32,426 --> 00:01:33,621
I wanted to save you both.

28
00:01:33,827 --> 00:01:36,296
Yeah. But you could
only save one of us.

29
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:39,500
That's why you
told Tetch to kill Lee,

30
00:01:39,833 --> 00:01:42,029
because you knew he
would do the opposite.

31
00:01:44,004 --> 00:01:48,032
Oldest trick in the book. At
least tell me you caught him.

32
00:01:48,575 --> 00:01:49,575
He's still in the wind.

33
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:54,077
Listen, Vale, it's
not what you think.

34
00:01:54,481 --> 00:01:55,710
It is.

35
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:58,885
You love Lee.

36
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,221
Which means we're done.

37
00:02:14,034 --> 00:02:16,003
- If there's anything I can do...
<i>- No.</i>

38
00:02:16,637 --> 00:02:18,469
No. Tetch was right.

39
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:21,237
You're nothing but trouble.

40
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,520
So, let me get this straight,

41
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:40,252
you're about to be in
possession of some kind of virus?

42
00:02:40,927 --> 00:02:42,054
(CHUCKLES LIGHTLY) Yes.

43
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:45,792
It's blood-based and can
be a little unpredictable.

44
00:02:46,299 --> 00:02:48,894
It can take weeks for
symptoms to manifest.

45
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:50,898
(SHUSHING) Oh.

46
00:02:51,772 --> 00:02:55,868
This is an accelerant.

47
00:02:56,109 --> 00:02:57,668
Mix it with the blood.

48
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,642
Wham! Bam! (MIMICS EXPLOSION)

49
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:02,873
That virus will hit him like a
semi going 90. (CHUCKLES)

50
00:03:06,453 --> 00:03:08,547
Oh. (CHUCKLES)

51
00:03:08,889 --> 00:03:10,221
The Red Queen.

52
00:03:10,724 --> 00:03:13,694
She's a blend of
psychotropic plants.

53
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,400
(GRUNTS) Thought
she'd be a big hit.

54
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:17,969
Turns out she's only good at
putting people in the looney bin.

55
00:03:18,065 --> 00:03:19,226
- I'll take her.
- (STUTTERS)

56
00:03:19,499 --> 00:03:21,798
That stuff's no joke.

57
00:03:22,169 --> 00:03:25,970
At first, it incapacitates you.
Then an hour into the trip,

58
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:27,986
(VOCALIZES) it
completely fries your brain.

59
00:03:28,175 --> 00:03:29,175
Perfect.

60
00:03:29,509 --> 00:03:32,968
I'm looking to sideline someone
before this evening's event.

61
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:34,180
(SCOFFS)

62
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:35,609
That'll do it. (CHUCKLES)

63
00:03:36,516 --> 00:03:40,180
Hey, uh, what exactly
are you planning?

64
00:03:42,022 --> 00:03:43,022
(CHOKES)

65
00:03:45,192 --> 00:03:47,320
(GASPING)

66
00:03:47,861 --> 00:03:54,563
This city tore my love from me,
so I'm plunging it into insanity.

67
00:03:54,868 --> 00:03:56,837
(YELLING)

68
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:59,062
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

69
00:04:05,445 --> 00:04:07,744
ISABELLA: <i>And that's where
I discovered my love of books.</i>

70
00:04:07,948 --> 00:04:08,948
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

71
00:04:09,182 --> 00:04:13,119
I never thought a fractured tibia
would launch my library career, but it did.

72
00:04:13,386 --> 00:04:15,878
Fun fact, the tibia is the
second largest bone in the body.

73
00:04:16,123 --> 00:04:17,989
Second only to the femur.

74
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:22,756
You have exquisite femurs.

75
00:04:22,996 --> 00:04:23,996
(CHUCKLES)

76
00:04:30,871 --> 00:04:31,930
PAPER BOY: Morning!

77
00:04:32,572 --> 00:04:35,371
- Oh. (CHUCKLES)
- Morning paper. What time is it?

78
00:04:35,675 --> 00:04:37,371
Oh, uh, it's just past 6:00.

79
00:04:41,882 --> 00:04:43,544
(CLEARS THROAT) Um, Edward,

80
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:48,251
these past 12 hours have
been the best of my life.

81
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,588
When can we meet again?

82
00:04:52,826 --> 00:04:54,590
What can't you have
for breakfast or lunch?

83
00:04:55,061 --> 00:04:57,360
Dinner. I'd love to.

84
00:04:57,597 --> 00:04:58,597
Delightful.

85
00:04:58,832 --> 00:05:00,392
Meet me at the
mayor's mansion at 8:00.

86
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,484
I understand that one is
expected to wait 24 hours

87
00:05:23,690 --> 00:05:27,092
before filing a missing person's
report, but, sir, I am the mayor!

88
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:30,387
Oswald. I am so sorry.

89
00:05:30,597 --> 00:05:31,597
(GASPS)

90
00:05:32,866 --> 00:05:35,563
When you didn't come
home, I assumed the worst.

91
00:05:35,902 --> 00:05:38,064
(LAUGHS) I'm so
glad you're okay.

92
00:05:38,405 --> 00:05:39,771
I'm better than okay.

93
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,373
I met someone.

94
00:05:44,244 --> 00:05:46,008
I think I'm in love! (LAUGHS)

95
00:05:56,957 --> 00:05:57,957
(BEEPS)

96
00:05:59,226 --> 00:06:01,718
Hey! Hey, you
can't be down here.

97
00:06:03,396 --> 00:06:04,396
Oh, I disagree.

98
00:06:04,664 --> 00:06:05,664
(GRUNTS)

99
00:06:17,444 --> 00:06:19,436
I don't understand why
we're doing all this, boss.

100
00:06:19,746 --> 00:06:22,215
Wasn't plugging
Gordon's girlfriend enough?

101
00:06:22,449 --> 00:06:25,476
Jim Gordon wasn't the only one
responsible for my sister's death.

102
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:31,548
Gotham ripped Alice from my
loving arms and turned her against me.

103
00:06:32,259 --> 00:06:34,888
What better way
to make this city pay

104
00:06:35,161 --> 00:06:39,257
than by spreading my
dear, dead sister's legacy.

105
00:06:47,274 --> 00:06:49,175
Oh, Alice.

106
00:07:04,991 --> 00:07:06,084
(OVEN TIMER DINGS)

107
00:07:11,665 --> 00:07:14,157
<i>Well. It's quite the operation
you've got going on in here.</i>

108
00:07:14,367 --> 00:07:15,391
Isn't it, Master Bruce?

109
00:07:16,336 --> 00:07:18,669
- Do you need a hand?
- I got it.

110
00:07:19,572 --> 00:07:23,236
Right. What time can
we expect Miss Kyle?

111
00:07:23,543 --> 00:07:24,943
6:00, I think.

112
00:07:25,245 --> 00:07:26,577
We'll see, won't we?

113
00:07:28,181 --> 00:07:31,515
She's coming, Alfred.
And, uh, Alfred...

114
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:35,714
Yes, yes, I know. I'll
make myself scarce.

115
00:07:35,989 --> 00:07:38,083
I'll give you all the
privacy that you need.

116
00:07:38,391 --> 00:07:39,450
Within earshot.

117
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:43,423
And the lights on.

118
00:07:52,539 --> 00:07:54,405
Well, I got bad news and worse.

119
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:55,901
Skip the preamble.

120
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,270
It was definitely Tetch
and his two dum-dums.

121
00:07:58,545 --> 00:08:00,377
And? What about Alice's body?

122
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:03,549
The eggheads here have had
her body on ice since it arrived.

123
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:07,352
Her blood's frozen, but still viable.
The second Tetch heats it up...

124
00:08:07,587 --> 00:08:08,987
He has himself the virus.

125
00:08:10,423 --> 00:08:11,903
How the hell did
he even get in here?

126
00:08:12,058 --> 00:08:14,323
The old-fashioned way.
Somebody let him in.

127
00:08:14,627 --> 00:08:17,028
I got an unconscious lab
tech and a missing guard.

128
00:08:17,364 --> 00:08:19,026
My money's on the guard.

129
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:21,231
Shouldn't you be in
the hospital with Vale?

130
00:08:21,534 --> 00:08:22,814
She's fine. Give me the rundown.

131
00:08:23,203 --> 00:08:25,502
Oh, so I take it you're
rejoining the force?

132
00:08:26,206 --> 00:08:29,438
I just want to help. There's no
reason I need to be a cop to do that.

133
00:08:29,709 --> 00:08:32,406
Well, as long as I'm
captain of the GCPD, you do.

134
00:08:32,712 --> 00:08:34,476
I'm tired of giving you slack.

135
00:08:34,781 --> 00:08:38,548
Get the hell off my crime scene
before I throw your ass in lock-up.

136
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:44,188
Biehls, Alban, escort
Mr. Gordon off of the premises.

137
00:08:44,491 --> 00:08:47,086
If he resists, book
him for obstruction.

138
00:08:47,827 --> 00:08:49,455
I'll go on my own.

139
00:08:52,132 --> 00:08:53,725
No, hey, hey, hey! Uh-uh. No.

140
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,600
I see that look in your eye. Do
not try to solve this by yourself.

141
00:08:56,803 --> 00:08:57,862
Then help me.

142
00:08:58,138 --> 00:09:00,178
If Tetch has Alice's blood,
we don't have much time.

143
00:09:00,407 --> 00:09:01,466
No. I'm not gonna aid you

144
00:09:01,674 --> 00:09:04,269
on one of your solo, bull crap,
kamikaze missions anymore!

145
00:09:04,511 --> 00:09:05,991
Tetch murdered
four people yesterday.

146
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:08,024
He shot Vale. I can't just
let him get away with it.

147
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:10,108
Nobody's asking you
to. But, Barnes is right.

148
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:14,320
Either be a cop, or don't.
What're you so afraid of?

149
00:09:15,321 --> 00:09:18,382
Is that what you
think? That I'm afraid?

150
00:09:19,826 --> 00:09:22,421
You know, you should go
to the hospital. Be with Vale.

151
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:26,325
And let those of us who wanna
wear the badge do our damn jobs.

152
00:09:32,138 --> 00:09:35,836
You are going to cut quite the fine
figure at the Founders' dinner tonight.

153
00:09:36,076 --> 00:09:37,169
Yes.

154
00:09:37,777 --> 00:09:39,177
Did you know that this dinner

155
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:42,177
has been thrown annually
for over 200 years?

156
00:09:42,482 --> 00:09:44,610
It was started by the
first families of Gotham.

157
00:09:45,151 --> 00:09:47,882
Only the most powerful
citizens are invited.

158
00:09:49,656 --> 00:09:51,386
It's a shame I don't
have a plus one.

159
00:09:51,791 --> 00:09:54,283
I can't go anyway.
I have a date.

160
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,274
With the woman you
claim to be in love with

161
00:09:56,496 --> 00:09:58,089
after only knowing
for a few hours?

162
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:00,165
Heart keeps its own time.

163
00:10:02,836 --> 00:10:04,134
I'm partial to the purple.

164
00:10:05,205 --> 00:10:07,401
The brocade brings out my eyes.

165
00:10:09,876 --> 00:10:12,107
Are you sure you aren't
mistaking infatuation for love?

166
00:10:12,312 --> 00:10:14,232
You did say she is the
spitting image of Kringle.

167
00:10:15,748 --> 00:10:18,843
Isabella's beautiful and smart.

168
00:10:19,886 --> 00:10:23,345
So, she bears a passing
resemblance to Kristen.

169
00:10:23,923 --> 00:10:25,448
It's just the
universe telling me...

170
00:10:26,159 --> 00:10:28,560
Telling me I have a
second chance at love.

171
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,726
Where did you say she works?

172
00:10:32,265 --> 00:10:33,858
The Main Public Library.

173
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:35,500
You're right about the brocade.

174
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,070
Do you mind if I skedaddle?

175
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,184
I just need to pick up
a few things for tonight.

176
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:44,174
Who am I to stand
in the way of love?

177
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:55,050
Missing guard from
the lab. Called in sick.

178
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:56,718
My gut says he's lying.

179
00:10:56,923 --> 00:11:01,258
Well, he's certainly no candidate
for sainthood. Gambling, petty theft...

180
00:11:01,528 --> 00:11:02,791
Might I have a word, Captain?

181
00:11:03,463 --> 00:11:05,694
Bring him in. What is it?

182
00:11:06,065 --> 00:11:08,665
I just heard from the head of
virology at the Biomedical facility.

183
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:11,247
Is this is about the tests they're
running on Alice's Tetch's blood?

184
00:11:11,271 --> 00:11:13,349
- Yes, in the first trial...
- One of the rats ran off the rails

185
00:11:13,373 --> 00:11:15,535
and murdered the rest. I
know. Doc Thompkins told me.

186
00:11:15,775 --> 00:11:18,006
But, uh, she thought it
might've been an anomaly.

187
00:11:18,244 --> 00:11:20,179
I'm afraid the second
study proves otherwise.

188
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,441
As in the first study, the rats
showed increased strength and agility.

189
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:28,883
But, by week two, the rats
were exhibiting manic tendencies.

190
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:30,282
<i>Violent rage.</i>

191
00:11:30,557 --> 00:11:33,755
By the study's end, every trace of
their original demeanor had vanished.

192
00:11:35,061 --> 00:11:37,155
I assume they're,
uh, working on a cure.

193
00:11:37,397 --> 00:11:39,423
Yes, but it could take years.

194
00:11:39,666 --> 00:11:42,431
Well, we only have
hours. Damn it!

195
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:45,065
If this virus gets set free...

196
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:50,601
- We have to find Tetch. Now.
- Yes, sir.

197
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:03,990
JERVIS: <i>Watch closely, Dumfree.</i>

198
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:06,654
<i>Isn't science marvelous?</i>

199
00:12:08,094 --> 00:12:11,462
Gravity, a few
heaters and voila!

200
00:12:11,931 --> 00:12:17,495
The last drops of coagulated
blood become cocktail mix.

201
00:12:24,544 --> 00:12:25,568
<i>Ah!</i>

202
00:12:26,145 --> 00:12:27,841
<i>Bravo, Alice.</i>

203
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:32,348
Truly, your best work.

204
00:12:43,463 --> 00:12:45,023
- You're kidding me.
- Please calm down.

205
00:12:45,064 --> 00:12:46,088
He said, "Kill Lee?"

206
00:12:46,332 --> 00:12:47,356
He knew Tetch wouldn't.

207
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,967
How? How could he
possibly have known that?

208
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:52,171
Somehow he got
inside Tetch's head,

209
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:55,431
and he knew that he would do
the opposite of what he told him to.

210
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:59,941
I see. So, why would Gordon offer up the
woman he's dating in place of my fiancée?

211
00:13:00,213 --> 00:13:01,340
Mario. Stop it.

212
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:04,641
We have so much to be thankful
for. I just want to move past this.

213
00:13:06,085 --> 00:13:07,212
Fine.

214
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:10,434
But, Jim Gordon's the reason
you were in danger, to begin with.

215
00:13:11,057 --> 00:13:12,525
I want him out of our lives.

216
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:14,193
Of course.

217
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:23,430
I came by to bring this to Vale.

218
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:25,568
(PAGER BEEPING)

219
00:13:26,873 --> 00:13:28,341
I got to get back to the ER.

220
00:13:42,088 --> 00:13:43,283
He's angry.

221
00:13:44,023 --> 00:13:45,389
I get that.

222
00:13:47,093 --> 00:13:48,584
He has every reason to be.

223
00:13:48,895 --> 00:13:50,921
I figured you'd be out
chasing down Tetch.

224
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:52,959
Barnes banned me.

225
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,332
No badge, no investigation.

226
00:13:55,635 --> 00:13:57,467
That's never stopped you before.

227
00:13:58,037 --> 00:14:00,836
They closed ranks. Even Bullock.

228
00:14:02,775 --> 00:14:06,075
He says I'm refusing the
badge because I'm afraid.

229
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:12,179
Jim, I know what
you did last night.

230
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:16,254
When you told Tetch to kill me,
you knew he would shoot Vale.

231
00:14:17,590 --> 00:14:19,923
No. I'm sorry. That's not true.

232
00:14:21,561 --> 00:14:23,401
At least have the decency
to be honest with me.

233
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:26,829
I am being honest. I
wanted to save Vale.

234
00:14:28,801 --> 00:14:31,930
Bullock was right,
you are afraid.

235
00:14:47,487 --> 00:14:48,511
(BELL DINGS)

236
00:14:54,127 --> 00:14:55,127
Hello there. (SCOFFS)

237
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:58,456
Mr. Mayor. What an
honor. How can I help you?

238
00:14:59,198 --> 00:15:01,429
I am attending the
Founders' dinner this evening,

239
00:15:01,868 --> 00:15:05,396
and I wanted to brush up on the
history of Gotham's first families.

240
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,869
- Hmm.
- My Chief of Staff suggested I come here.

241
00:15:09,475 --> 00:15:11,273
I think you might know him.

242
00:15:12,145 --> 00:15:13,875
Yes. I know Edward.

243
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,480
We just met.

244
00:15:16,282 --> 00:15:18,080
But... (SIGHS)

245
00:15:18,651 --> 00:15:21,485
Well, I feel I've known
him my whole life.

246
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:24,451
- How romantic.
- Oh.

247
00:15:25,057 --> 00:15:28,186
Listen to me blathering
on. You wanted a book?

248
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:34,626
I'm so glad you appreciate Ed.

249
00:15:36,869 --> 00:15:38,098
(ISABELLA CHUCKLES)

250
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:41,639
Really, I should thank you
for brightening Ed's spirits.

251
00:15:43,476 --> 00:15:47,811
He has been so down
since he got out of Arkham.

252
00:15:53,186 --> 00:15:55,121
Edward was in Arkham?

253
00:15:56,389 --> 00:15:57,389
You don't know.

254
00:15:58,891 --> 00:16:00,723
It was front page news.

255
00:16:00,927 --> 00:16:02,486
I stick to books.

256
00:16:03,029 --> 00:16:06,625
Don't people typically
go to Arkham for murder?

257
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:11,335
I make it a policy not to
gossip about staff, but...

258
00:16:12,171 --> 00:16:13,332
(MOUTHING) Yes.

259
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,640
(SCOFFS)

260
00:16:24,784 --> 00:16:26,810
Uncanny how much
you look like her.

261
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:31,321
It's that swan-like neck.

262
00:16:32,625 --> 00:16:33,625
Mmm-hmm.

263
00:16:33,793 --> 00:16:35,386
Ed loves a neck.

264
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:37,463
(LAUGHS)

265
00:16:38,264 --> 00:16:41,996
Well, thank you for the book.
It was a pleasure meeting you.

266
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,165
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

267
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:09,422
Hey! Hey!

268
00:17:10,830 --> 00:17:11,830
Hey!

269
00:17:13,633 --> 00:17:15,693
JERVIS: <i>The tea
party was part one.</i>

270
00:17:16,569 --> 00:17:18,561
I want to have a lot more fun.

271
00:17:26,012 --> 00:17:27,480
<i>I had my way with you.</i>

272
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:31,081
<i>Now Gotham's up for round two.</i>

273
00:17:32,318 --> 00:17:33,758
What the hell are
you talking about?

274
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:36,947
JERVIS: <i>Why, I'm going to
dismantle your beloved city</i>

275
00:17:37,323 --> 00:17:39,986
<i>from the top on down.</i>

276
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:41,960
(CHOKES)

277
00:17:45,765 --> 00:17:48,234
And you can't stop me.

278
00:17:50,336 --> 00:17:51,861
<i>Enjoy the trip.</i>

279
00:17:52,772 --> 00:17:55,003
<i>It's going to be a bumpy ride.</i>

280
00:17:59,378 --> 00:18:01,813
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

281
00:18:19,065 --> 00:18:20,089
Watch where you're going.

282
00:18:21,367 --> 00:18:23,302
Of course, Mr. Mayor.

283
00:18:23,669 --> 00:18:24,932
So sorry.

284
00:18:26,973 --> 00:18:28,134
Cretin.

285
00:18:46,425 --> 00:18:48,860
(OVERLAPPING INDISTINCT CHATTER)

286
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:56,234
(ECHOING) Jim.

287
00:18:59,038 --> 00:19:00,802
Jim...

288
00:19:02,441 --> 00:19:03,534
Jim!

289
00:19:05,077 --> 00:19:07,410
Finally sleeping beauty stirs.

290
00:19:08,948 --> 00:19:09,948
Where am I?

291
00:19:10,216 --> 00:19:11,616
<i>You got dosed, buttercup.</i>

292
00:19:11,884 --> 00:19:13,409
Welcome to your hallucination.

293
00:19:16,489 --> 00:19:17,548
What are you doing in it?

294
00:19:18,057 --> 00:19:19,116
Hell, if I know.

295
00:19:19,525 --> 00:19:22,256
Now, we've got a
lot be getting on with.

296
00:19:22,628 --> 00:19:23,708
I don't have time for this.

297
00:19:24,463 --> 00:19:25,463
Ow!

298
00:19:26,365 --> 00:19:28,834
See, that's the thing
about hallucinations, Jimbo.

299
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:32,301
You got to ride out
the trip. Bummer, huh?

300
00:19:33,372 --> 00:19:34,840
(ELEVATOR WHIRRING)

301
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:39,702
What exactly
does this trip entail?

302
00:19:39,945 --> 00:19:41,538
Well, no one gave
me an itinerary.

303
00:19:41,781 --> 00:19:44,250
But, knowing what
goes on inside your head,

304
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:46,885
I'm sure it'll be a chock full
of belly laughs. (LAUGHS)

305
00:19:47,953 --> 00:19:51,014
Just kidding. We all
know fun isn't your forte.

306
00:19:51,557 --> 00:19:52,923
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

307
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,321
This is where I face
my inner demons, huh?

308
00:19:57,163 --> 00:19:58,597
That's up to you.

309
00:20:03,269 --> 00:20:07,206
Well, go on. Unless you wanna
stay in this tiny space with me.

310
00:20:08,774 --> 00:20:10,572
I'll take my chances.

311
00:20:18,951 --> 00:20:20,943
BRUCE: (ECHOING) <i>Jim...</i>

312
00:20:21,587 --> 00:20:22,953
<i>Jim...</i>

313
00:20:27,159 --> 00:20:30,459
Jim... Jim...

314
00:20:33,532 --> 00:20:34,532
Bruce?

315
00:20:35,034 --> 00:20:36,434
You don't have much time.

316
00:20:37,036 --> 00:20:38,231
What are you talking about?

317
00:20:38,604 --> 00:20:40,163
You don't have much time.

318
00:20:40,439 --> 00:20:42,874
Bruce! Bruce.

319
00:20:43,109 --> 00:20:44,109
(GRUNTS)

320
00:20:46,011 --> 00:20:47,570
- (PANTING)
- (GUNSHOTS FIRING)

321
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:52,614
- Where did Bruce go?
- (BOMB EXPLODING)

322
00:20:55,354 --> 00:20:57,880
(SPEAKING GIBBERISH)

323
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:01,784
What?

324
00:21:03,829 --> 00:21:05,991
Never leave your unit behind.

325
00:21:07,466 --> 00:21:09,367
(COBBLEPOT HUMMING)

326
00:21:09,668 --> 00:21:11,330
I have to find him.

327
00:21:11,871 --> 00:21:13,169
(GUNSHOTS FIRING AT A DISTANCE)

328
00:21:13,506 --> 00:21:14,940
(COBBLEPOT CONTINUES HUMMING)

329
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:20,208
Bruce! Bruce!

330
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:26,041
I'm glad you came.

331
00:21:26,685 --> 00:21:29,621
What did you mean when you
said I didn't have much time?

332
00:21:29,922 --> 00:21:33,723
I just wanted you to follow
me so I could show you that.

333
00:21:36,362 --> 00:21:37,386
<i>Down there.</i>

334
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:39,061
(MAN SCREAMING)

335
00:21:39,331 --> 00:21:40,822
<i>It's because of you.</i>

336
00:21:42,368 --> 00:21:43,893
(PEOPLE MOANING AND GROANING)

337
00:21:44,236 --> 00:21:45,829
<i>Congratulations, Jim.</i>

338
00:21:46,071 --> 00:21:49,599
You did it. You're the hero
you always dreamed of being.

339
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,536
Bruce... Don't.

340
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,620
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

341
00:22:19,038 --> 00:22:20,301
(SCREAMING)

342
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:22,474
Your name was on the schedule.

343
00:22:22,708 --> 00:22:25,200
Yeah, I told you. It was
my shift at the Bio-Lab,

344
00:22:25,444 --> 00:22:27,044
but I came down with
something. (COUGHS)

345
00:22:27,112 --> 00:22:30,173
The only thing you're coming down
with, pal, is 10 years at Blackgate.

346
00:22:30,416 --> 00:22:33,614
Hey, hey, hey. That's no
way to treat a sick man.

347
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:38,452
Listen, Sullivan, Tetch got in
using an employee's key card.

348
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:40,451
Just show us your card
and you're free to go.

349
00:22:40,726 --> 00:22:43,355
Screw you. I want a lawyer.

350
00:22:44,997 --> 00:22:45,997
(CHUCKLES)

351
00:22:47,166 --> 00:22:49,465
You pigs think you're
such tough guys.

352
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:51,600
(GROANING)

353
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:54,568
Honest citizens driven mad.

354
00:22:55,541 --> 00:22:58,443
Tearing each other limb from
limb just because you decided

355
00:22:58,677 --> 00:23:01,647
that this city's security
is not your concern.

356
00:23:02,715 --> 00:23:04,355
Tell us what you know
about Jervis Tetch.

357
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,280
Tell us what you know
about Jervis Tetch.

358
00:23:06,518 --> 00:23:08,453
Captain! Captain!

359
00:23:08,754 --> 00:23:11,553
Hey. I thought I was supposed
to be the bad cop here.

360
00:23:11,991 --> 00:23:13,391
<i>A bruiser in a wrestling mask</i>

361
00:23:13,726 --> 00:23:16,059
paid me to hand over my
key card and take the day off.

362
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:17,863
Promised I wouldn't
get in trouble.

363
00:23:18,097 --> 00:23:21,556
Said the cops would be too
busy taking back control of the city.

364
00:23:22,101 --> 00:23:25,037
And? Tell us something
that might actually help.

365
00:23:25,838 --> 00:23:27,807
He was driving a catering van.

366
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:29,974
Why would the Tweeds
need a catering van?

367
00:23:31,043 --> 00:23:33,103
Wait. What's the date?

368
00:23:33,445 --> 00:23:34,640
Friday.

369
00:23:35,881 --> 00:23:36,905
The date.

370
00:23:37,383 --> 00:23:38,476
The 27th.

371
00:23:39,051 --> 00:23:40,383
The Founders' dinner.

372
00:23:40,619 --> 00:23:43,953
The Archbishop, the Comptroller,
the Mayor all in the same place.

373
00:23:44,823 --> 00:23:48,021
Put together a unit. And
not a word to Gordon.

374
00:23:55,834 --> 00:23:59,327
JERVIS: A drop of
blood in each wine glass

375
00:24:00,539 --> 00:24:04,203
makes mad men
of the ruling class.

376
00:24:19,224 --> 00:24:20,817
(BARBARA BLOWING)

377
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:22,627
(JIM COUGHS)

378
00:24:24,530 --> 00:24:25,657
What the hell are you doing?

379
00:24:25,898 --> 00:24:28,458
Saving your life.
Like you wanted.

380
00:24:29,368 --> 00:24:31,462
The last thing I want is
your lips on my mouth.

381
00:24:32,204 --> 00:24:35,436
Newsflash. Everything that
is happening is in your head.

382
00:24:35,674 --> 00:24:37,609
Which means you
made me give you CPR.

383
00:24:37,843 --> 00:24:41,837
Just like you put me in this
really cheesy nurse's uniform.

384
00:24:42,414 --> 00:24:43,848
That's easily rectified.

385
00:24:44,750 --> 00:24:46,116
(CHUCKLES)

386
00:24:46,385 --> 00:24:49,253
Seriously? One bad
encounter with Bruce...

387
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:50,786
I don't want to talk about it.

388
00:24:51,023 --> 00:24:54,255
Fine. Just don't fall into a
monosyllabic depression because...

389
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:55,484
(ELEVATOR HALTS)

390
00:24:55,694 --> 00:24:59,790
We're at the next stop. I have
mixed feelings about this floor.

391
00:25:02,768 --> 00:25:04,202
I'm afraid to ask.

392
00:25:08,774 --> 00:25:12,267
(INDISTINCT SINGING)

393
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:21,551
I'm so glad you're home. Mom
thought you were gonna be late.

394
00:25:22,154 --> 00:25:25,124
Ha! Mom owes me a quarter. Mom.

395
00:25:26,392 --> 00:25:28,452
We made a bet that
you were gonna be late.

396
00:25:28,794 --> 00:25:33,323
Frankie had more faith than I did.
Now go on. Take those rolls to the table.

397
00:25:35,601 --> 00:25:36,625
How was your trip?

398
00:25:40,439 --> 00:25:41,907
Earth to Jim.

399
00:25:43,509 --> 00:25:44,509
(JIM SIGHS)

400
00:25:46,412 --> 00:25:48,506
I'm sorry. You just
look so beautiful.

401
00:25:48,747 --> 00:25:50,443
Ew. You guys are gross.

402
00:25:52,151 --> 00:25:55,713
Julie, one day, you're gonna love
somebody as much as I love your father.

403
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,581
- Never. Boys are dumb.
- Are not.

404
00:26:06,799 --> 00:26:08,529
You feeling okay, honey?

405
00:26:11,637 --> 00:26:14,038
I'm just glad to be
here. With you guys.

406
00:26:15,841 --> 00:26:17,207
I love you so much.

407
00:26:20,145 --> 00:26:21,875
Does that mean we can get a dog?

408
00:26:22,314 --> 00:26:25,773
You two. Does that
mean we can get a dog?

409
00:26:28,821 --> 00:26:31,848
- Sure. (CHUCKLES)
- Yay! You're the best, Dad.

410
00:26:33,959 --> 00:26:35,427
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

411
00:26:39,865 --> 00:26:41,128
The best.

412
00:26:46,772 --> 00:26:48,673
Just the best, Jim.

413
00:26:48,907 --> 00:26:50,899
No. No, no, no, no! Come back.

414
00:26:58,250 --> 00:26:59,809
You look like you need a drink.

415
00:27:03,856 --> 00:27:04,856
(YELLS)

416
00:27:05,324 --> 00:27:06,417
- Jim.
- (GRUNTS)

417
00:27:07,359 --> 00:27:10,955
Open the damn gate, Barbara. I
need to get back to them. To her.

418
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:17,381
If you're so desperate to have
Thompkins and the two kids,

419
00:27:17,503 --> 00:27:19,802
why're you in that crappy
apartment playing Private Dick?

420
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:22,665
Let go of me. You don't know
what the hell you're talking about.

421
00:27:22,941 --> 00:27:25,570
I know you're lost. You
wanna find your way home?

422
00:27:25,811 --> 00:27:27,211
Play nice.

423
00:27:33,185 --> 00:27:35,017
It's a long way to the basement.

424
00:27:48,333 --> 00:27:50,529
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

425
00:27:54,273 --> 00:27:58,335
So, the little minx
was a no-show?

426
00:27:59,778 --> 00:28:03,112
Well, it seems a frightful shame to
let this beautiful meal go to waste.

427
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:05,875
What say you, we wrap it up,
and have it for lunch tomorrow?

428
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:08,352
Eh?

429
00:28:13,025 --> 00:28:14,926
You always bring your
butler along on dates?

430
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:26,430
Right. I'll leave you to it.

431
00:28:27,639 --> 00:28:29,130
Excuse me, miss.

432
00:28:31,577 --> 00:28:32,875
You're late.

433
00:28:33,979 --> 00:28:37,245
Stuff came up. Chill.

434
00:28:39,284 --> 00:28:40,752
Alfred really out did himself.

435
00:28:41,053 --> 00:28:43,318
I made all of it. For you.

436
00:28:44,289 --> 00:28:45,587
What's with the attitude?

437
00:28:46,792 --> 00:28:48,055
You stood me up.

438
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:49,820
I got busy.

439
00:28:50,095 --> 00:28:52,291
Selina, if we're gonna do this,

440
00:28:52,698 --> 00:28:56,430
whatever this is, I need
you to be honest with me.

441
00:29:01,006 --> 00:29:03,407
This, me and you...

442
00:29:05,677 --> 00:29:09,512
It's weird for me. Okay?

443
00:29:10,949 --> 00:29:12,850
It's weird for me.

444
00:29:14,886 --> 00:29:16,821
It's weird for me, too.

445
00:29:17,623 --> 00:29:20,252
So, you gonna cut
the cake or what?

446
00:29:21,293 --> 00:29:22,352
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

447
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:31,497
Of course, I didn't want to
stand in the way of love, but...

448
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:33,762
This woman would've
been a disaster.

449
00:29:34,006 --> 00:29:36,908
It sounds as if you
did your friend a favor.

450
00:29:37,843 --> 00:29:41,803
I'm sorry, I have been talking so
much. I never asked your name.

451
00:29:42,748 --> 00:29:44,011
Kathryn.

452
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:46,474
Just Kathryn?

453
00:29:46,852 --> 00:29:48,047
- Mmm-hmm.
- (CHUCKLES)

454
00:29:49,721 --> 00:29:51,485
How did you end up
at the Founders' dinner?

455
00:29:51,757 --> 00:29:54,090
- If it's not rude of me to ask.
- Not at all.

456
00:29:54,693 --> 00:29:57,492
I'm from one of
Gotham's oldest families.

457
00:29:58,497 --> 00:30:03,128
And I'm part of a group
which oversees things.

458
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:06,199
What sort of things?

459
00:30:06,772 --> 00:30:09,037
Everything that
matters in Gotham.

460
00:30:10,175 --> 00:30:14,135
We've had our eye on you
for some time, Mr. Cobblepot.

461
00:30:15,514 --> 00:30:17,210
- Who exactly are you?
- (BELL DINGING)

462
00:30:20,252 --> 00:30:23,051
We'll contact you
when the time is right.

463
00:30:24,690 --> 00:30:26,352
Enjoy your evening.

464
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:45,800
Excuse me, did you
notice the rather severe

465
00:30:46,044 --> 00:30:48,513
looking woman I was speaking
with? She said her name...

466
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,943
(PEOPLE GASPING AND YELLING)

467
00:30:51,683 --> 00:30:53,675
What is this? What is going on?

468
00:30:53,952 --> 00:30:56,888
I'm afraid your evening has
been hijacked, Mr. Mayor.

469
00:30:57,289 --> 00:31:00,191
- (PANTING)
- I see the champagne didn't leave a mark.

470
00:31:00,792 --> 00:31:02,124
I'm so glad.

471
00:31:02,828 --> 00:31:04,524
For those of you
who don't know me.

472
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:07,295
My name is Jervis Tetch.

473
00:31:08,300 --> 00:31:10,360
<i>I promise not to take
up too much of your time.</i>

474
00:31:10,602 --> 00:31:13,538
But the fact is, you are
the heads of Gotham.

475
00:31:14,005 --> 00:31:15,005
And tonight.

476
00:31:15,774 --> 00:31:18,005
The heads of Gotham will roll.

477
00:31:19,845 --> 00:31:20,845
But first,

478
00:31:22,347 --> 00:31:23,406
a toast.

479
00:31:23,749 --> 00:31:26,218
A drink, to your health.

480
00:31:26,918 --> 00:31:28,284
And if we don't?

481
00:31:29,454 --> 00:31:31,889
Change, my friends, is nigh.

482
00:31:32,157 --> 00:31:35,719
Drink the wine, or else you die.

483
00:31:36,294 --> 00:31:37,294
(GRUNTS)

484
00:31:44,736 --> 00:31:47,296
Glasses down now! Glasses down!

485
00:31:47,572 --> 00:31:49,268
(PEOPLE YELLING)

486
00:31:49,641 --> 00:31:51,007
(GRUNTING)

487
00:31:52,677 --> 00:31:54,202
(GROANING)

488
00:31:57,349 --> 00:31:58,442
JERVIS: <i>Oh, my!</i>

489
00:31:59,050 --> 00:32:01,451
Is that my dear sister I see?

490
00:32:03,655 --> 00:32:05,624
She's in you, isn't
she? (LAUGHS)

491
00:32:07,092 --> 00:32:08,890
What fun! (LAUGHS)

492
00:32:09,828 --> 00:32:11,854
What fun! (GRUNTS)

493
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:15,496
- Shut up! Shut up!
- (LAUGHING)

494
00:32:21,907 --> 00:32:23,466
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

495
00:32:24,709 --> 00:32:26,041
Last stop.

496
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:29,846
Don't be scared.

497
00:32:35,754 --> 00:32:38,189
It's not easy to face
who you really are.

498
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:43,122
I should know.

499
00:32:47,065 --> 00:32:50,365
Do you ever wish you were
the person you used to be?

500
00:32:53,872 --> 00:32:55,067
Do you?

501
00:33:08,854 --> 00:33:10,083
Use this.

502
00:33:13,225 --> 00:33:16,423
Or don't. It's up to you.

503
00:33:19,764 --> 00:33:21,289
Good luck, Jim.

504
00:33:47,926 --> 00:33:48,950
Sir?

505
00:33:51,329 --> 00:33:52,388
Sir.

506
00:33:52,831 --> 00:33:54,231
You looking for this?

507
00:33:58,670 --> 00:34:02,732
- Dad?
- Hey! It's good to see you, son.

508
00:34:04,276 --> 00:34:06,507
I'm always losing
that darn thing.

509
00:34:09,614 --> 00:34:10,854
<i>Get in. We don't wanna be late.</i>

510
00:34:12,551 --> 00:34:16,511
FEMALE NURSE: <i>Doctor. Doctor.
Some help. Doctor, he's unconscious.</i>

511
00:34:17,088 --> 00:34:21,583
- Doctor Calvi, he's in here.
- Jim? Jim?

512
00:34:22,460 --> 00:34:23,519
<i>This was beside him.</i>

513
00:34:26,131 --> 00:34:28,691
"Red Queen." I've heard of this.

514
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:30,647
Give me twenty 20
CCs of Haloperidol.

515
00:34:30,835 --> 00:34:31,859
Right away, Doctor.

516
00:34:32,103 --> 00:34:35,699
Jim? Can you hear me? Jim! Jim?

517
00:34:40,278 --> 00:34:44,238
Come on, Jimmy. It's time to go.

518
00:35:03,969 --> 00:35:05,767
- Something wrong?
- No.

519
00:35:07,806 --> 00:35:10,503
I'm just glad to see
you. I missed you a lot.

520
00:35:10,809 --> 00:35:12,607
No, sorry I haven't
been around more.

521
00:35:12,911 --> 00:35:15,881
I heard you got into some kind of
trouble. You want to talk about it?

522
00:35:18,717 --> 00:35:22,085
When I was a kid,
people would tell me.

523
00:35:22,520 --> 00:35:24,148
"Your dad's a hero."

524
00:35:25,957 --> 00:35:28,238
All I knew is you went to
court every day and every night,

525
00:35:28,326 --> 00:35:31,785
you came home and you played
ball with me while Mom made dinner.

526
00:35:33,264 --> 00:35:34,892
Then I got older.

527
00:35:36,167 --> 00:35:38,500
And I understood
you were a hero.

528
00:35:40,271 --> 00:35:43,833
Only, for me, it wasn't just
that you'd been a great DA.

529
00:35:45,243 --> 00:35:47,940
It was that you got
up, day after day.

530
00:35:49,247 --> 00:35:51,148
You faced down the
worst this city had to offer,

531
00:35:51,449 --> 00:35:54,442
but you never brought
that home to Mom and me.

532
00:35:55,387 --> 00:35:57,015
You protected us.

533
00:35:59,357 --> 00:36:01,724
I wanted to be just like you.

534
00:36:05,130 --> 00:36:07,292
Turns out, I'm the opposite.

535
00:36:08,299 --> 00:36:10,666
I destroy everything
and everyone around me.

536
00:36:10,902 --> 00:36:14,737
No. Come on, Jimmy.
I'm far from perfect.

537
00:36:15,940 --> 00:36:18,774
I've got plenty of darkness
inside me. I just don't dwell on it.

538
00:36:19,044 --> 00:36:20,964
Focus on the good you
can do. That's what counts.

539
00:36:21,212 --> 00:36:22,805
- That's what I'm trying to do.
- No.

540
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:25,946
You've been hiding behind
self-righteous, lone wolf nonsense

541
00:36:26,217 --> 00:36:28,118
because you're afraid.

542
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:30,011
Why is that?

543
00:36:30,755 --> 00:36:34,749
The badge holds expectations.
People want a hero. And I'm not.

544
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:38,527
You know what makes a hero, son?

545
00:36:39,164 --> 00:36:42,328
A man who values protecting
others above protecting himself.

546
00:36:42,600 --> 00:36:44,645
A man who knows his
limits, but isn't afraid to fail.

547
00:36:44,669 --> 00:36:47,070
A man who knows when to
ask for help when he needs it.

548
00:36:47,372 --> 00:36:48,772
Now, (CHUCKLES)

549
00:36:48,940 --> 00:36:52,206
I wasn't always that man. But,
damn, it didn't stop me from trying.

550
00:36:53,812 --> 00:36:56,646
- I don't know how to be that man.
- Sure you do.

551
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:59,176
Just got to follow the code.

552
00:37:00,652 --> 00:37:01,847
You remember what that is?

553
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:04,054
No.

554
00:37:04,289 --> 00:37:06,087
The code we Gordons
promise to live by?

555
00:37:06,524 --> 00:37:07,958
No. Why can't I remember?

556
00:37:08,727 --> 00:37:10,593
Because you're lost, son.

557
00:37:11,062 --> 00:37:12,462
You wanna find
your way back home?

558
00:37:12,731 --> 00:37:15,530
The answer you're
looking for is in my ring.

559
00:37:17,102 --> 00:37:20,197
Ah, shoot! It's
time for me to go.

560
00:37:20,839 --> 00:37:22,102
No. I want to talk to you more.

561
00:37:22,407 --> 00:37:23,875
I can't. Someone's
coming for me.

562
00:37:24,209 --> 00:37:26,906
- No. Dad... No, Dad, please, don't go.
- (VEHICLE HONKING)

563
00:37:27,178 --> 00:37:28,456
- No. Dad.
- I'm proud of you, Jimmy.

564
00:37:28,480 --> 00:37:29,520
<i>- Dad!</i>
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

565
00:37:30,448 --> 00:37:31,575
Jim...

566
00:37:32,717 --> 00:37:34,413
Jim, can you hear me? Jim?

567
00:37:34,986 --> 00:37:36,045
Yeah.

568
00:37:37,422 --> 00:37:39,254
Yeah, I can hear you.

569
00:37:40,759 --> 00:37:41,759
(GROANS)

570
00:37:42,794 --> 00:37:48,563
It's Haloperidol, antipsychotic. You were
dosed with a pretty powerful hallucinogen.

571
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:50,725
- It was Tetch.
- I know.

572
00:37:51,035 --> 00:37:53,504
Someone saw him
leaving the hospital.

573
00:37:53,738 --> 00:37:57,505
You know, you're lucky. Another
minute, we would've lost you.

574
00:38:00,345 --> 00:38:01,813
Thank you.

575
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:03,137
It's my job.

576
00:38:03,414 --> 00:38:06,316
FEMALE NURSE: <i>Doctor Calvi?
We need your signature, please.</i>

577
00:38:06,484 --> 00:38:07,484
Uh-huh.

578
00:38:08,153 --> 00:38:10,213
I'll get somebody
to take IV out.

579
00:38:10,555 --> 00:38:14,617
Half an hour, glass of orange
juice, you'll be good to go.

580
00:38:29,407 --> 00:38:31,103
So, while I did...

581
00:38:31,843 --> 00:38:33,744
Kill my girlfriend...

582
00:38:34,679 --> 00:38:38,707
Who does look rather similar to
you. It was not out of malice or intent.

583
00:38:39,017 --> 00:38:41,282
It was an accident
that I deeply regret.

584
00:38:41,553 --> 00:38:43,230
And I was not gonna
tell you this, but then...

585
00:38:43,254 --> 00:38:44,415
Edward,

586
00:38:45,156 --> 00:38:46,749
I know what you did.

587
00:38:47,759 --> 00:38:48,920
You do?

588
00:38:49,594 --> 00:38:53,053
I spent the afternoon reading
every article about you.

589
00:38:53,998 --> 00:38:58,436
You know what I did and yet,
you still came on this date anyway?

590
00:38:59,771 --> 00:39:00,771
Well...

591
00:39:01,606 --> 00:39:03,040
That's not logical.

592
00:39:03,474 --> 00:39:05,443
Love isn't logical.

593
00:39:10,381 --> 00:39:13,647
I've lived my whole life
inside the pages of books.

594
00:39:15,386 --> 00:39:17,878
Any other men I've dated,

595
00:39:18,823 --> 00:39:22,282
they didn't compare to the
lovers I spent my life with.

596
00:39:23,328 --> 00:39:24,694
Antony.

597
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:26,492
Cleopatra.

598
00:39:27,065 --> 00:39:28,533
Romeo and Juliet.

599
00:39:30,235 --> 00:39:32,932
Othello, Desdemona...

600
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:36,000
All of whom died.

601
00:39:37,108 --> 00:39:38,269
Edward.

602
00:39:39,077 --> 00:39:41,376
You're the first to measure up.

603
00:39:42,614 --> 00:39:44,742
You're the one I waited for.

604
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:47,477
- You're not scared of me?
- (CHUCKLES)

605
00:39:48,019 --> 00:39:49,385
Of course I am.

606
00:39:50,722 --> 00:39:52,486
Can you feel how fast
my heart's beating?

607
00:40:04,535 --> 00:40:07,334
Well, Ed, you would
not believe the night...

608
00:40:08,439 --> 00:40:09,737
Oswald, good evening.

609
00:40:12,777 --> 00:40:14,405
This is Isabella.

610
00:40:17,782 --> 00:40:19,717
We have met. (CHUCKLES)

611
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:25,289
Would you excuse
me? I am very tired.

612
00:41:08,499 --> 00:41:11,936
<i>"Dum spiramus tuebimur."</i>

613
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:21,071
"While we breathe,
we shall defend."

614
00:41:31,456 --> 00:41:32,947
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

615
00:41:34,859 --> 00:41:35,952
Come in.

616
00:41:36,761 --> 00:41:37,820
You busy?

617
00:41:38,029 --> 00:41:40,021
Just finishing up some
paperwork on Tetch.

618
00:41:40,765 --> 00:41:42,700
He and the Tweeds are
safe and sound in Arkham.

619
00:41:43,101 --> 00:41:44,981
Hopefully, that's the
last we'll hear from them.

620
00:41:45,436 --> 00:41:46,597
Congratulations.

621
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:50,471
You did what I
couldn't. I mean that.

622
00:41:50,775 --> 00:41:53,404
A humble Jim Gordon.
What do you know?

623
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:58,313
I hear Tetch sent
you on quite a trip.

624
00:41:58,616 --> 00:42:00,881
If it wasn't for
Mario, I'd be dead.

625
00:42:01,452 --> 00:42:03,785
Anyway, I'm not here about that.

626
00:42:07,258 --> 00:42:09,284
I want to rejoin the GCPD.

627
00:42:11,562 --> 00:42:13,758
Why the sudden change of heart?

628
00:42:15,199 --> 00:42:17,998
I made a promise to
someone when I was younger.

629
00:42:20,238 --> 00:42:22,503
I intend to keep that promise.

630
00:42:26,911 --> 00:42:28,004
Good.

631
00:42:29,313 --> 00:42:30,474
<i>We need you here.</i>

632
00:42:31,682 --> 00:42:32,980
I need you here.

633
00:42:36,087 --> 00:42:37,248
Welcome back, Detective.

634
00:42:44,996 --> 00:42:47,556
MAN: <i>It seems you
left dinner just in time.</i>

635
00:42:48,266 --> 00:42:49,427
Indeed.

636
00:42:50,668 --> 00:42:52,864
And what did you
think of our new mayor?

637
00:42:53,304 --> 00:42:57,105
My gut says "Once a
criminal, always a criminal."

638
00:42:58,676 --> 00:43:00,110
Well, keep an eye on him.

639
00:43:02,547 --> 00:43:04,675
Judgment is coming, Kathryn.

640
00:43:07,218 --> 00:43:08,743
For all of us.

641
00:43:19,664 --> 00:43:21,656
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

642
00:43:54,532 --> 00:43:55,532
English -SDH
